This plugin bundles or derives from the following third-party work.

1. shadcn/ui (MIT) — https://github.com/shadcn-ui/ui
   The base-color token values under scripts/palettes/*.json are copied from the
   public registry at https://ui.shadcn.com/r/colors/<name>.json (cssVarsV4).
   Refresh them with `node scripts/refresh-palettes.mjs`.

2. Tailwind CSS (MIT) — https://github.com/tailwindlabs/tailwindcss
   The status token values (green, amber, red) are the oklch values published in
   the Tailwind v4 default theme.

3. Geist and Geist Mono (SIL Open Font License 1.1) — https://github.com/vercel/geist-font
   Scaffolded projects install the `geist` npm package, which self-hosts these
   fonts. The fonts are not redistributed by this repository.
   License: https://github.com/vercel/geist-font/blob/main/LICENSE.TXT

4. Display fonts installed on request through `@fontsource-variable/<name>`
   (https://fontsource.org) keep their own upstream licenses, usually the SIL
   Open Font License. The plugin installs them into your project; it does not
   redistribute font files.

5. Aceternity UI and Magic UI components are NOT bundled or redistributed here.
   When you ask for one, it is installed straight from its own registry into
   your project with the shadcn CLI, and remains subject to its own license:
   - Magic UI: MIT — https://github.com/magicuidesign/magicui
   - Aceternity UI: see https://ui.aceternity.com/licence — the published terms
     cover Aceternity UI Pro and forbid redistributing the source or bundling it
     into templates or kits. Check the terms yourself before commercial use.

6. Blocks (templates/blocks/) are written for this kit. They import libraries
   that the blocks skill installs into your project and that are not
   redistributed here: TanStack Table (MIT), Recharts (MIT), react-hook-form
   (MIT), Zod (MIT), @hookform/resolvers (MIT), lucide-react (ISC), and shadcn/ui
   components (MIT) added with the shadcn CLI.

7. Test fixtures under tests/fixtures/registry/ record only the metadata that
   `shadcn view` returns for Magic UI and Aceternity items (names, dependencies,
   CSS variables, file paths). File contents are short stand-ins written for the
   tests, not the original source.

